---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro'
const title = 'Veqtor Workspace documentation — Local document tools'
const description = 'The four Workspace tools, task copies, local execution, saving and optional Word diagnostics. Connection instructions and earlier MCP documentation.'
const tools = [
  {name:'workspace_info', description:'Returns the connection capabilities and document workflow. Start here so the assistant has the current editing recipe.'},
  {name:'document_task', description:'Starts a task from a saved file, reports its state and saves the working copy. One task represents one document-editing request.'},
  {name:'run_python', description:'Runs model-written Python with selected read paths and a writable working area. It can also read selected documents without starting an editing task.'},
  {name:'check_docx', description:'Optionally compares a candidate Word document with the original and reports findings and unchecked areas. It is not a required save gate.'},
]
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/docs">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Documentation" title="How Workspace handles a document task." lede="Veqtor Workspace is a local MCP server. The connected model chooses how to read, edit and verify the document; Workspace controls the task copies, local execution and saving." breadcrumbs={[{label:'Documentation'}]} compact />
  <section class="section"><div class="shell prose-shell"><article class="prose">
    <h2 id="tools">Four tools</h2>
    <div class="tool-list">{tools.map(tool => <article><code>{tool.name}</code><p>{tool.description}</p></article>)}</div>
    <h2 id="connection">Connection</h2><p>Use the <a href="/setup">installation guide</a> for Claude Desktop and ChatGPT Desktop. Codex CLI and the IDE extension can use the same local command. Workspace does not include a model or a hosted account service.</p>
    <h2 id="tasks">Reading and editing</h2><p>A reading-only request can use <code>run_python(read_paths=[...])</code>. For an edit, <code>document_task(action="start", file="/absolute/path/to/document.docx")</code> snapshots the current on-disk file and gives the model a private working copy. Supporting paths are selected from the user’s instructions.</p><p>The model writes the editing code. Reading helpers and document checks are optional. Ask explicitly for tracked changes, comments, a clean copy or retention of existing revisions; those choices are not automatically inferred as a fixed editing mode.</p>
    <h2 id="saving">Saving</h2><p><code>document_task(action="save", task_id="...")</code> replaces the selected file after checking it against the task’s starting snapshot. An explicit new <code>file</code> path creates a separate result in an existing folder; an existing destination is not overwritten. Save-as uses the task snapshot even if the original has since changed.</p><p>Unsaved Word edits cannot be read or detected. Avoid simultaneous editing and reopen the file in Word after saving. This is not an atomic cross-application lock.</p><p>If a save is interrupted, inspect the task status before retrying. It can report <code>saved</code>, <code>saved_then_changed</code>, <code>not_saved</code> or <code>outcome_unknown</code>. A missing reply does not prove that the file was not saved.</p>
    <h2 id="checks">Optional checks</h2><p><code>check_docx</code> can identify mismatches after reversing new tracked changes and comments. Findings need interpretation against the requested task. Authorized acceptance of revisions or removal of comments can intentionally change the baseline.</p><p>The diagnostic does not open Microsoft Word, certify legal wording or guarantee formatting and field behavior. A clean report is not required to save. Optional rendering requires an available renderer and may paginate differently from Word.</p>
    <h2 id="boundary">Local execution and storage</h2><p>The Python runner has selected file and runtime reads, writes in its task area and no network access. These restrictions do not make the whole assistant offline. Content returned through tools enters the AI conversation.</p><p>Snapshots and logs remain in private local application storage. There is no automatic cleanup. Keep this data confidential along with the source documents.</p>
    <h2 id="previous">Earlier Veqtor MCP</h2><p>The fourteen-tool Veqtor MCP 0.5 contract is a different product. Its published package and tagged documentation remain linked from the <a href="/veqtor-mcp">earlier product page</a>.</p>
  </article><aside class="side-index"><strong>On this page</strong><a href="#tools">Four tools</a><a href="#connection">Connection</a><a href="#tasks">Document tasks</a><a href="#saving">Saving</a><a href="#checks">Checks</a><a href="#boundary">Local boundary</a><a href="/security">Security</a><a href="/limitations">Limitations</a></aside></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>.tool-list article { padding: 20px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); } .tool-list code { color: var(--violet-strong); } .tool-list p { margin-bottom: 0; }</style>
